{"kind":"artifact","text":"Dual-era MCP service with the three reviewed defects repaired, unmerged on branch task/mcp-dual-era at 7d15ec89. All three findings from ca10c0cb were correct and all three were mine. The P1 is fixed: initialize was handled before the era was consulted, so a connection that had already spoken modern could flip itself to legacy and thereafter omit the per-request metadata the modern revision requires, which is precisely the invariant the previous commit message claimed to establish; the opening now selects the era once and initialize is refused after a modern request without disturbing the era. The first P2 is fixed: the initialize decoder's error was discarded and no field was validated, so a handshake with empty params latched legacy and enabled bare tools/list; protocolVersion, capabilities, and clientInfo.name are now required, wrong types and undecodable params are rejected with -32602, and any failure leaves the era undetermined so the client may open again. The second P2 is fixed: server/discover returned the modern envelope to legacy connections, contradicting the stated rule that legacy results carry neither envelope nor cache directives; it belongs to the modern revision and is now unavailable on what a legacy client negotiated. Each defect carries a regression test, and each test was confirmed to fail against 3c4588b0 and pass against this head rather than merely asserted to; the malformed-handshake case is table-driven over empty params, each missing required field, an empty version, and wrong types. make vet, make test, and go test -race ./... pass. Not reviewed at this head and not merged.","body":{"commit":"7d15ec891f0e1bcc66968de97465e453bc0e3b2b","path":"spike/cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}